    "engine": "knitr",
    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"Hands-on Exercise 7a\"\nsubtitle: \"Modelling, Visualising and Analysing Network Data with R\"\nauthor: \"Jedidiah Asaf T\"\nformat:\n  html:\n    toc: true\n    toc-depth: 3\n    code-fold: true\n---\n\n## Overview\n\nThis hands-on exercise recreates the key techniques from Chapter 27 of *R for Visual Analytics*. Using the GAStech email corpus, it models the organisation as a **graph** and visualises it with `tidygraph` + `ggraph` (static) and `visNetwork` (interactive), including centrality-based node sizing.\n\n## Setup\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nif (!require(pacman)) install.packages(\"pacman\")\n\npacman::p_load(\n  igraph, tidygraph, ggraph, visNetwork,\n  lubridate, graphlayouts, ggforce, tidyverse\n)\n\nGAStech_nodes <- read_csv(\"data/GAStech_email_node.csv\")\nGAStech_edges <- read_csv(\"data/GAStech_email_edge-v2.csv\")\n```\n:::\n\n\n## Data Wrangling\n\nThe send date is parsed and the weekday derived. Edges are then aggregated to weighted, work-related links between different people.\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nGAStech_edges <- GAStech_edges %>%\n  mutate(SendDate = dmy(SentDate)) %>%\n  mutate(Weekday = wday(SendDate, label = TRUE, abbr = FALSE))\n\nGAStech_edges_aggregated <- GAStech_edges %>%\n  filter(MainSubject == \"Work related\") %>%\n  group_by(source, target, Weekday) %>%\n  summarise(Weight = n(), .groups = \"drop\") %>%\n  filter(source != target) %>%\n  filter(Weight > 1)\n```\n:::\n\n\n# 1. Building the Graph Object\n\n`tbl_graph()` combines the node and edge tables into a `tidygraph` object.\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nGAStech_graph <- tbl_graph(\n  nodes = GAStech_nodes,\n  edges = GAStech_edges_aggregated,\n  directed = TRUE\n)\n\nGAStech_graph\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n\n```\n# A tbl_graph: 54 nodes and 1456 edges\n#\n# A directed multigraph with 1 component\n#\n# Node Data: 54 × 4 (active)\n      id label               Department     Title                               \n   <dbl> <chr>               <chr>          <chr>                               \n 1     1 Mat.Bramar          Administration Assistant to CEO                    \n 2     2 Anda.Ribera         Administration Assistant to CFO                    \n 3     3 Rachel.Pantanal     Administration Assistant to CIO                    \n 4     4 Linda.Lagos         Administration Assistant to COO                    \n 5     5 Ruscella.Mies.Haber Administration Assistant to Engineering Group Mana…\n 6     6 Carla.Forluniau     Administration Assistant to IT Group Manager       \n 7     7 Cornelia.Lais       Administration Assistant to Security Group Manager \n 8    44 Kanon.Herrero       Security       Badging Office                      \n 9    45 Varja.Lagos         Security       Badging Office                      \n10    46 Stenig.Fusil        Security       Building Control                    \n# ℹ 44 more rows\n#\n# Edge Data: 1,456 × 4\n   from    to Weekday   Weight\n  <int> <int> <ord>      <int>\n1     1     2 Monday         4\n2     1     2 Tuesday        3\n3     1     2 Wednesday      5\n# ℹ 1,453 more rows\n```\n\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\n# 2. Static Network with ggraph\n\n## 2.1 Basic Plot\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nggraph(GAStech_graph, layout = \"nicely\") +\n  geom_edge_link(aes(width = Weight), alpha = 0.2) +\n  scale_edge_width(range = c(0.1, 5)) +\n  geom_node_point(aes(colour = Department), size = 3) +\n  theme_graph()\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n![](hands_on_exercise_7a_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-4-1.png){width=864}\n:::\n:::\n\n\n## 2.2 Faceting by Weekday\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nggraph(GAStech_graph, layout = \"nicely\") +\n  geom_edge_link(aes(width = Weight), alpha = 0.2) +\n  scale_edge_width(range = c(0.1, 5)) +\n  geom_node_point(aes(colour = Department), size = 2) +\n  facet_edges(~ Weekday) +\n  theme_graph(foreground = \"grey80\", fg_text_colour = \"white\")\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n![](hands_on_exercise_7a_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-5-1.png){width=1056}\n:::\n:::\n\n\n## 2.3 Sizing Nodes by Betweenness Centrality\n\nBetweenness centrality highlights the people who act as bridges in the communication network.\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nGAStech_graph <- GAStech_graph %>%\n  mutate(betweenness_centrality = centrality_betweenness())\n\nggraph(GAStech_graph, layout = \"fr\") +\n  geom_edge_link(aes(width = Weight), alpha = 0.2) +\n  scale_edge_width(range = c(0.1, 5)) +\n  geom_node_point(aes(colour = Department, size = betweenness_centrality)) +\n  theme_graph()\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n![](hands_on_exercise_7a_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-6-1.png){width=864}\n:::\n:::\n\n\n## 2.4 Detecting Communities\n\n`tidygraph` inherits `igraph`'s community-detection algorithms via its `group_*` functions. Here `group_edge_betweenness()` partitions the graph into communities, which are then mapped to node colour.\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\ng <- GAStech_graph %>%\n  mutate(community = as.factor(\n    group_edge_betweenness(\n      weights = Weight,\n      directed = TRUE))) %>%\n  ggraph(layout = \"fr\") +\n  geom_edge_link(aes(width = Weight), alpha = 0.2) +\n  scale_edge_width(range = c(0.1, 5)) +\n  geom_node_point(aes(colour = community))\n\ng + theme_graph()\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n![](hands_on_exercise_7a_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-7-1.png){width=864}\n:::\n:::\n\n\nTo make communities easier to read, `geom_mark_hull()` (from `ggforce`) draws a hull around each community found by `group_optimal()`, while nodes are still coloured by `Department` and sized by betweenness centrality.\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\ng <- GAStech_graph %>%\n  activate(nodes) %>%\n  mutate(community = as.factor(\n    group_optimal(weights = Weight)),\n    betweenness_measure = centrality_betweenness()) %>%\n  ggraph(layout = \"fr\") +\n  geom_mark_hull(\n    aes(x, y,\n        group = community,\n        fill = community),\n    alpha = 0.2,\n    expand = unit(0.3, \"cm\"),\n    radius = unit(0.3, \"cm\")\n  ) +\n  geom_edge_link(aes(width = Weight), alpha = 0.2) +\n  scale_edge_width(range = c(0.1, 5)) +\n  geom_node_point(aes(fill = Department,\n                      size = betweenness_measure),\n                  color = \"black\",\n                  shape = 21)\n\ng + theme_graph()\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n![](hands_on_exercise_7a_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-8-1.png){width=864}\n:::\n:::\n\n\n# 3. Interactive Network with visNetwork\n\n`visNetwork` expects the columns `from` and `to`; the aggregated edges are renamed accordingly.\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nGAStech_edges_vis <- GAStech_edges_aggregated %>%\n  rename(from = source, to = target)\n\nvisNetwork(GAStech_nodes, GAStech_edges_vis) %>%\n  visIgraphLayout(layout = \"layout_with_fr\") %>%\n  visOptions(\n    highlightNearest = list(enabled = TRUE, degree = 1, hover = TRUE),\n    nodesIdSelection = TRUE\n  ) %>%\n  visLegend() %>%\n  visLayout(randomSeed = 123)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"visNetwork html-widget html-fill-item\" id=\"htmlwidget-f77dd71bde5668518ba3\" style=\"width:100%;height:464px;\"></div>\n<script type=\"application/json\" data-for=\"htmlwidget-f77dd71bde5668518ba3\">{\"x\":{\"nodes\":{\"id\":[1,2,3,4,5,6,7,44,45,46,8,9,10,11,12,13,14,15,16,21,26,17,18,19,20,39,40,41,42,43,27,28,29,47,48,49,50,22,51,52,53,54,23,24,25,30,31,32,33,34,35,36,37,38],\"label\":[\"Mat.Bramar\",\"Anda.Ribera\",\"Rachel.Pantanal\",\"Linda.Lagos\",\"Ruscella.Mies.Haber\",\"Carla.Forluniau\",\"Cornelia.Lais\",\"Kanon.Herrero\",\"Varja.Lagos\",\"Stenig.Fusil\",\"Marin.Onda\",\"Axel.Calzas\",\"Brand.Tempestad\",\"Elsa.Orilla\",\"Isande.Borrasca\",\"Kare.Orilla\",\"Felix.Balas\",\"Lars.Azada\",\"Lidelse.Dedos\",\"Willem.Vasco-Pais\",\"Bertrand.Ovan\",\"Adra.Nubarron\",\"Birgitta.Frente\",\"Gustav.Cazar\",\"Vira.Frente\",\"Linnea.Bergen\",\"Lucas.Alcaza